+---
+id: task-001-spring-newsletter-discount-codes
+type: task
+title: "Spring newsletter discount codes"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Spring newsletter discount codes
+
+## Request
+
+The spring campaign sends discount codes in the newsletter. A customer can give one code to an order.
+
+- `SPRING10`: 10 % off the order's items, rounded to the nearest cent, a half cent rounding up.
+- `WELCOME5`: 5.00 € off the order's items, only on an order whose items come to 30.00 € or more.
+
+## Rules
+
+- An order takes one code at most. A second code replaces the first.
+- An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on an order under 30.00 €, is refused with an error that says why. The order is
+  left as it was.
+- The discount never touches shipping. Whether an order ships free is decided on its items before any discount.
+- The order book offers `applyCode(orderNumber, code)`.
+- An order's totals show the discount as `discountCents` (0 without a code), and `totalCents` is items minus
+  discount plus shipping.
+
+## Choices made here
+
+- The `WELCOME5` threshold is checked on the items before the discount, the same basis as free shipping.
+- An unknown code is refused with `not-found`. A code that does not fit the order (`WELCOME5` below 30.00 €) is
+  refused with `invalid`.
+- The discount is computed in integer cents: `floor((items × 10 + 50) / 100)` for `SPRING10`.
+- Applying a code does not change the order's stored lines. The applied code is kept beside the order, not added to
+  its record.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `applyCode` on a known order with `SPRING10` gives `discountCents` = 10 % of items, rounded half up.
+- `applyCode` with `WELCOME5` gives 500 cents off on items of 3000 cents or more, and is refused below that, with
+  the order unchanged.
+- An unknown code, or an unknown order number, is refused, with an error message.
+- A second code replaces the first. A refused code keeps the previous code.
+- Shipping is the same with or without a code: free when items are 50.00 € or more, otherwise 4.90 €.
+- `totalCents` = `itemsCents` − `discountCents` + `shippingCents`, with `discountCents` 0 when no code is applied.
+- Existing order tests still pass, with the totals shape updated for `discountCents`.
+- The changelog records the change.
